## Comprehensive Analysis: ArcCreate Reference Implementation

Based on my exploration of the ArcCreate source code, here's how it handles the three key areas you requested:

---

### 1. **Background Image Rendering & Scaling**

**File Paths:**
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/GameplayData.cs` - Background sprite management
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Skin/SkinService.cs` - Skin and background coordination
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Skin/Options/AlignmentOption.cs` - Default background asset
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Camera/CameraService.cs` - Screen resolution handling
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scenes/Gameplay.unity` - Scene hierarchy with background GameObject

**Key Implementation Details:**

**Background Loading (GameplayData.cs, lines 145-169):**
- Loads background image as PNG/JPG via `File.ReadAllBytes(path)` 
- Creates Texture2D with `TextureWrapMode.Clamp` wrapping mode
- Creates Sprite with `Sprite.Create(texture, new Rect(0, 0, t.width, t.height), pivot: (0.5f, 0.5f))`
- Stores in `public State<Sprite> Background` property
- Falls back to default alignment skin background if load fails

**Default Background (AlignmentOption.cs):**
- Each alignment skin has a `[SerializeField] public Sprite defaultBackground` asset
- Wrapped in `ExternalSprite DefaultBackground` for dynamic loading
- Used when no custom background is loaded

**Screen Resolution Tracking (CameraService.cs, lines 61-77):**
- **AspectAdjustment calculation:** `float height = backgroundCamera.pixelHeight / (backgroundCamera.pixelWidth / 16f); float adjustment = (height - 9) / 3f;`
  - This normalizes 16:9 aspect ratio to 0, and tablet (4:3/16:12) aspect ratio to 1
  - Used for dynamic camera property interpolation

- **Background Canvas Positioning (UpdateBackgroundCanvas, lines 243-248):**
  ```csharp
  backgroundRect.pivot = new Vector2(0.5f, Mathf.Lerp(0.87f, 0.5f, AspectAdjustment));
  backgroundRect.anchorMin = new Vector2(0.5f, Mathf.Lerp(1f, 0.5f, AspectAdjustment));
  backgroundRect.anchorMax = new Vector2(0.5f, Mathf.Lerp(1f, 0.5f, AspectAdjustment));
  ```
  - For 16:9 screens: Pivot (0.5, 0.87), Anchors at top (1.0)
  - For tablet: Pivot (0.5, 0.5), Anchors centered (0.5)
  - This anchors and scales the background differently based on aspect ratio

**Camera FOV Scaling (CameraService.cs, lines 76-77):**
- Field of View: `Mathf.Lerp(50, 65, AspectAdjustment)` - widens FOV for tablet aspect ratios

**No explicit aspect ratio fill mode:**
- The background sprite is displayed using a SpriteRenderer with the sprite's native resolution
- Scaling/stretching is handled via RectTransform size and anchor settings on the canvas
- The image fills the background rect created by the camera viewport

---

### 2. **UI Rendering for Gameplay Elements (Top-Right Corner)**

**File Paths:**
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Scenecontrol/Controllers/Scene.cs` - Main scene controller with all UI elements
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Scenecontrol/Controllers/Internal/InfoPanelController.cs` - Info panel (score, grade, jacket, etc.)
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Scenecontrol/Controllers/Common/ImageController.cs` - Image positioning/scaling
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Scenecontrol/Controllers/Common/CanvasController.cs` - Canvas configuration

**UI Element Hierarchy (Scene.cs, lines 32-182):**
```
Scene
├── Combo (TextController) - Line 32-40
├── Score Title (TextController) - Line 42-50  
├── Score (TextController) - Line 52-60
├── Predicted Grade (TextController) - Line 62-80
├── Jacket Art (ImageController) - Line 92-100
├── Title (TitleController) - Line 102-110
├── Composer (ComposerController) - Line 112-120
├── Difficulty Text (DifficultyController) - Line 122-141
├── Info Panel (InfoPanelController) - Line 153-161 [contains score display]
├── Pause Button (ImageController) - Line 163-171
├── Background (ImageController) - Line 173-181
└── HUD Canvas (CanvasController) - Line 142-151
```

**InfoPanelController (lines 12-113 in InfoPanelController.cs):**
```csharp
[SerializeField] private TextController scoreTitle;      // "SCORE" label
[SerializeField] private TextController score;            // Score number
[SerializeField] private TextController predictedGrade;   // Letter grade
[SerializeField] private ImageController jacket;          // Jacket art display
[SerializeField] private TitleController title;           // Song title
[SerializeField] private ComposerController composer;    // Composer name
[SerializeField] private DifficultyController difficultyText; // Difficulty level
```

**Positioning System (ImageController.cs & CanvasController.cs):**

**RectTransform Properties (Controllers store these as modifiable channels):**
- **Position:** `translationX/Y/Z` (anchoredPosition3D)
- **Rotation:** `rotationX/Y/Z` (localRotation)
- **Scale:** `scaleX/Y/Z` (localScale)
- **Anchoring:** `anchorMinX/Y`, `anchorMaxX/Y` - Relative to parent rect
- **Pivot:** `pivotX/Y` - Rotation/scale origin point
- **Size:** `rectW`, `rectH` - Width and height

**UpdateRect method (ImageController.cs, lines 356-363):**
```csharp
public void UpdateRect(float w, float h, Vector2 anchorMin, Vector2 anchorMax, Vector2 pivot)
{
    rectTransform.anchorMin = anchorMin;
    rectTransform.anchorMax = anchorMax;
    rectTransform.pivot = pivot;
    rectTransform.SetSizeWithCurrentAnchors(RectTransform.Axis.Horizontal, w);
    rectTransform.SetSizeWithCurrentAnchors(RectTransform.Axis.Vertical, h);
}
```

**UpdatePosition method (ImageController.cs, lines 348-353):**
```csharp
public void UpdatePosition(Vector3 translation, Quaternion rotation, Vector3 scale)
{
    rectTransform.anchoredPosition3D = translation;
    rectTransform.localScale = scale;
    rectTransform.localRotation = rotation;
}
```

**Screen Size Context (Gameplay/Utility/Values.cs, lines 113-119):**
```csharp
public static Vector2 ScreenSize { get; set; } = Vector2.one;     // Current screen pixel size
public static Vector2 ScreenSizeBase { get; set; } = Vector2.one; // Reference resolution
public static float LaneScreenHitboxHorizontal => LaneScreenHitboxBase.x * ScreenSize.x / ScreenSizeBase.x;
public static float LaneScreenHitboxVertical => LaneScreenHitboxBase.y * ScreenSize.y / ScreenSizeBase.y;
```

**Screen Size Tracking (GameplayManager.cs, line 55):**
```csharp
Values.ScreenSize = new Vector2(backgroundCamera.pixelWidth, backgroundCamera.pixelHeight);
```

**Screen Resolution Channels (Lua scripting):**
- `ScreenWidthChannel.cs` - Returns `Services.Camera.GameplayCamera.pixelWidth`
- `ScreenHeightChannel.cs` - Returns `Services.Camera.GameplayCamera.pixelHeight`
- `ScreenIs16By9Channel.cs` - Returns 1 if 16:9 (threshold 0.1), else 0

---

### 3. **SkinService & Visual Management**

**File Path:**
- `/f/Code/better-arc/re/ArcCreate/Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/Skin/SkinService.cs` - Main skin management service

**Class Definition (lines 16-43):**
```csharp
public class SkinService : MonoBehaviour, ISkinService, ISkinControl
{
    [SerializeField] private SpriteRenderer singleLineL, singleLineR;
    [SerializeField] private TMP_Text comboText;
    [SerializeField] private SpriteRenderer track;
    [SerializeField] private SpriteRenderer[] criticalLines = new SpriteRenderer[4];
    [SerializeField] private Image infoPanel;
    [SerializeField] private Image pauseButton;
    [SerializeField] private VideoPlayer videoBackground;

    [SerializeField] private List<AlignmentOption> alignmentOptions;
    [SerializeField] private List<NoteSkinOption> noteSkinOptions;
    [SerializeField] private List<ParticleSkinOption> particleSkinOptions;
    [SerializeField] private List<TrackSkinOption> trackSkinOptions;
    [SerializeField] private List<AccentOption> accentOptions;
    [SerializeField] private List<SingleLineOption> singleLineOptions;
}
```

**Skin Properties (Public API):**
```csharp
public string AlignmentSkin { get; set; }      // Side view (left/right)
public string NoteSkin { get; set; }           // Tap/hold note appearance
public string ParticleSkin { get; set; }       // Hit particles
public string TrackSkin { get; set; }          // Lane/track graphics
public string SingleLineSkin { get; set; }     // Sky/single line
public string AccentSkin { get; set; }         // Combo text color, critical line
public Sprite DefaultBackground { get; }       // From alignment.DefaultBackground
public Color ComboColor { get; }               // Combo text color
```

**Background Handling (Line 215):**
```csharp
public Sprite DefaultBackground => currentAlignment.DefaultBackground.Value;
```

**Color Management (Lines 302-331):**
```csharp
public void SetArcColors(List<Color> arcs, List<Color> arcLows)
{
    // Applies colorblind mode if enabled
    if (Settings.EnableColorblind.Value && arcs[i] == defaultArcColors[i])
    {
        arcColors.Add(defaultArcColorblindColors[i]);
    }
}
```

**Accent/Combo Color (Lines 175-199):**
```csharp
public string AccentSkin
{
    set
    {
        AccentOption accentOpt = accentOptions.FirstOrDefault(opt => opt.Name == value);
        foreach (var c in criticalLines)
        {
            c.sprite = accentOpt.CriticalLineSkin.Value;
        }
        comboText.color = accentOpt.ComboColor;
        currentComboColor = accentOpt.ComboColor;
    }
}
```

**Video Background (Lines 377-392):**
```csharp
public void SetVideoBackground(string path, bool isUri)
{
    bool enabled = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(path) && !Settings.DisableAdvancedGraphics.Value;
    videoBackground.enabled = enabled;
    videoBackgroundRenderer.enabled = enabled;

    if (enabled)
    {
        videoBackground.url = isUri ? path : "file://" + path;
        // Android 29+ requires different path format
    }
}
```

**Material Management (Lines 296-337):**
- Shader property IDs: `_TraceColor`, `_ShadowColor`
- Materials instantiated in Awake() for runtime modification
- SetColor() called to update trace/shadow materials

---

### Summary

**Background Rendering:** Uses sprite rendering with RectTransform anchoring system that adapts to 16:9 vs tablet aspect ratios. Camera FOV and background canvas pivot/anchor points lerp based on aspect ratio calculation.

**UI Elements:** All positioned via RectTransform with modifiable anchor, pivot, size, position, rotation, and scale properties. Screen size tracked in Values.ScreenSize for relative scaling. Lua scripting can access pixel dimensions via screen context channels.

**SkinService:** Centralized service managing all visual elements (skins, colors, particles, background sprites). Supports colorblind mode, video backgrounds, and dynamic material reloading.

